WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.320
Hello, there.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.153
I'm Gav.
I'm Dan.

00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:03.530
We're The Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.772
Dan, the other day we had
a conversation, didn't we?

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.605
Yup.

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:08.240
And I was like, how can
we get two paint balls

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.790
to collide mid-air and
film it in slow motion?

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.400
My first thought was
we're just gonna stand

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.320
opposite each other and just let rip

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.600
and then hopefully...

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.860
Would never happen.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.450
The accuracy, the timing,
it would never happen.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.200
The pain, as well.
The pain, the fear.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.020
You'd be scared like this.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.624
I've had bad luck with paint balls.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.070
Ooh, that looks like a shot to the mouth.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.380
Gavin, you look like a mess.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.730
Bloody, dead eye rising, blew my face off.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.400
It looks like you have a second mouth.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.620
It's not pleasant.
It's not nice.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.290
So, instead, I've made this contraption

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.720
with vice grips and string.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.590
Yeah, I mean, it is a
complex thing for us,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.480
but in the grand scheme of
internet videos, it's very basic.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.320
I mean, there could be like

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.544
an electronic button to just do it,

00:00:51.544 --> 00:00:53.270
but instead I've just bought two guns

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.650
and sort of tried to rig them up

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.890
so they're shooting each other.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.200
Okay, so we'll see if we can collide

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.030
two paint balls somewhere around here.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.460
I'm gonna have to pre-set
the focus and the framing,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.480
but you know probably about
around there, isn't it?

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.040
We'll film it at 28,500
frames a second on the V2511

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.720
and if we're feeling a little bit cheeky,

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.310
we'll boost that frame rate up.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.210
Juicy.
And see what we can get.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.820
Juicy.
Juicy.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.970
So, somewhere around here, yeah?

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.290
Yeah.
Just like, all right.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.143
So, you're just eyeing it.

00:01:18.143 --> 00:01:20.250
I mean, it's so minuscule that

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.750
I'm gonna try and eye it, yeah.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.440
It's just kind of difficult because

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.600
sometimes when you clamp it back up,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.350
it just goes back where it wants.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:27.183
A little bit of give.

00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:29.890
Yeah, there's a bit of give
in the plastic of the gun.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.810
If we had, like a cylindrical rod,

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.860
we could just shove it down both barrels.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.240
It's true.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.920
We don't though.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.053
Yeah, if we were more
prepared, it'd be easier.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.860
Let's see how that does.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.813
You ready?
Yeah.

00:01:48.013 --> 00:01:48.846
No.

00:01:50.054 --> 00:01:50.887
No.

00:01:52.556 --> 00:01:53.389
No.

00:02:04.628 --> 00:02:05.490
Yup!

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.690
That was it?
Yup.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.440
Aw.
What's up?

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.508
I think they just bonked.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.353
They hit!

00:02:13.353 --> 00:02:14.700
Yeah, they did!

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.554
I think they just glanced
each other slightly.

00:02:16.554 --> 00:02:18.600
What are the chances of that?

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.065
Tell me when you're ready.
Ready.

00:02:22.615 --> 00:02:23.448
Yup.

00:02:25.243 --> 00:02:26.163
I think that hit.

00:02:27.171 --> 00:02:28.229
Whoa!

00:02:28.229 --> 00:02:30.860
Did the green one just annihilate it?

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.793
The green one survived!

00:02:32.793 --> 00:02:34.190
How's that happen?

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.860
It's different every time we do it!

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.940
It's just like when you
get hit in paint ball

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.130
and it doesn't explode.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.570
Is there, like, tape or
something on that paint ball?

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.770
No, it's like half of it's got

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.186
the branding pattern, I think, on it.

00:02:44.186 --> 00:02:45.530
A little bit of the pattern, sort of,

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.810
swung off and spun away.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.643
Look.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.480
Oh, yeah.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.850
Frisbee'd it into the distance.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.588
Okay, my first adjustment was too much

00:02:52.588 --> 00:02:54.430
and it meant that they just dinked.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.310
So, I've readjusted that time,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.870
and only one of them exploded,

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.740
and they weren't quite bang on.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.640
So, this time I've adjusted
again, just a little bit,

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.380
and hopefully we'll
get that exact meaty...

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.340
A little eek.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.400
Yeah.
A little gnats.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.593
Little eek and gnats.

00:03:08.482 --> 00:03:09.315
Gnats.

00:03:09.315 --> 00:03:11.306
A gnats kneecap, yeah,
that's the saying, isn't it?

00:03:11.306 --> 00:03:12.139
Yeah.

00:03:13.873 --> 00:03:14.706
Yup.

00:03:14.706 --> 00:03:15.890
That was it?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.723
I think so.

00:03:16.723 --> 00:03:19.894
I actually saw the exact second
that they hit each other.

00:03:21.035 --> 00:03:22.640
You know when you close your eyes

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.760
and you have like freeze-frame and clink?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.920
I captured that perfectly.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.060
I went like, boop, and
I just saw it explode.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.980
Could you send that to me?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:30.940
Yeah, yeah, hang on.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:31.830
Send the jpeg.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.720
All right.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.980
I've got airdrop turned on.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:35.813
Got it.

00:03:35.813 --> 00:03:36.910
Man, this camera's loud.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.016
All right, playing back.

00:03:39.154 --> 00:03:40.321
Here we go.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.676
Nailed it!

00:03:45.676 --> 00:03:46.690
Perfect!

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.657
That's amazing!

00:03:47.657 --> 00:03:49.502
So, it looks like they hit on the back,

00:03:49.502 --> 00:03:50.335
like one is on the front,
one is on the back.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.060
Yeah, just slightly.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:56.023
Look how they open up, like a fruit.

00:03:56.023 --> 00:03:58.400
It's like a physalis or
a kumquat or something.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.860
Yeah, in here it's like juicy

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.030
and then it turns into like a spiderweb.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.352
It almost looks like a
nervous system there,

00:04:03.352 --> 00:04:04.690
like a lot of neurons.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.730
Yeah, or like a capillaries, or something.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.320
Wonder how much that
actually happens in, like,

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.430
real paint ball matches?

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.640
It must happen quite a bit.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.473
Is that square on enough?

00:04:13.473 --> 00:04:14.660
Or would you want any more adjustments?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.640
That's pretty good.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.178
So satisfying, getting it the first time.

00:04:17.178 --> 00:04:18.240
Yeah.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.180
I thought these were made of rubber,

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.640
but they're actually made of, like,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.950
plastic that's quite thick.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.070
You can see the difference
in the paint balls.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.280
This one split along the actually--

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.820
Is that like, the seal hole?

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.400
Yeah, the two different kinds of plastic

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.420
that seal the paint in.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.860
And, this one, is just sort
of burst all over the place.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.880
I think these are the more expensive ones.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.995
And, these are the cheaper ones.

00:04:36.995 --> 00:04:38.550
Has it run out of gas?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.390
Yeah, we've run out of gas,

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:40.880
so they're sort of flopping out the gun,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.400
instead of firing out.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.237
Me, too.

00:04:43.237 --> 00:04:45.040
I need more beans.
Need more beans.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:45.873
How do you remove it

00:04:45.873 --> 00:04:46.920
without it spraying everywhere?

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.710
I don't know if you can.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:49.817
Sweaty hands, eh.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.280
Maybe I haven't run out of gas.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.273
Jesus!

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.975
Yup.

00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:09.160
Flipping A.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.074
That soaked me!

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.000
Sometimes it's hard to tell
when it actually happens.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.283
Yeah, makes you wonder
how many we've missed.

00:05:19.215 --> 00:05:20.048
The other one.

00:05:20.048 --> 00:05:21.391
Oh, .

00:05:23.153 --> 00:05:25.486
That is so satisfying.

00:05:25.486 --> 00:05:26.700
It's cool, isn't it?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.670
It's amazing that even though

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.280
one comes out way before the other,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.220
they still meet perfectly in focus.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.053
That's so weird.

00:05:32.053 --> 00:05:34.258
Is it just that I'm always
pulling one slightly later?

00:05:34.258 --> 00:05:35.091
I think so.

00:05:35.091 --> 00:05:36.470
I think it's just, there's a slight delay.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:37.303
So, I'm not--

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.380
Well, I mean, even if you do that,

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.790
in slow-mo, there's always gonna be

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.360
one that goes before the other.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.530
What an operation this is.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.363
I know.

00:05:43.363 --> 00:05:44.493
Yup.

00:05:44.493 --> 00:05:46.272
Yup.

00:05:46.272 --> 00:05:47.105
Yup.

00:05:47.105 --> 00:05:48.560
Excellent shooting.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:49.980
Thank you, very much, sir.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.279
Excellent shooting for you, too.

00:05:51.279 --> 00:05:52.112
Oh, thanks, thank you very much.

00:05:52.112 --> 00:05:56.983
Yeah.

00:06:39.403 --> 00:06:42.220
It's so weird, because
there's probably milliseconds

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.860
in the difference that
I'm pulling them there,

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.580
but in slow-mo, it just looks like an age.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.870
Like, it's halfway to the gun before

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:48.703
the green one even comes out.

00:06:48.703 --> 00:06:49.536
Well, let's count.

00:06:49.536 --> 00:06:51.620
So, that one's at the end of the barrel

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.620
at, well, it's 3:52:33 seconds .104231.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.260
Okay.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:01.500
So, what's the first number?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:02.510
That's the tenth of a second.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.360
What's the third number?
1000th.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.193
So, I'm 12 thousandths of a second out?

00:07:11.716 --> 00:07:13.520
You should be ashamed of yourself.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:14.552
Call myself a slow-mo guy.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.440
Made a mess of the board there.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.150
Oh, and the fence over here.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.480
The thing is, I figured that
this fence was further away

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.960
so the pattern would be a bit more spread.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.060
How long do you think it would take me

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.263
to paint the whole fence
with a paint ball gun?

00:07:31.233 --> 00:07:32.066
A week?

00:07:32.066 --> 00:07:33.240
A week?
Yeah.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.340
Like, solid, if it's going
bang bang bang bang bang.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.520
Wouldn't be very cost effective,

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.363
considering all the paint
balls and the CO2 you'd need.

00:07:38.363 --> 00:07:39.710
It's be a lot.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.180
I wonder how much that would cost.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.013
It's not very drippy, is it,

00:07:42.013 --> 00:07:43.893
and look, it's very powdery.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.493
Look, it's so weird.

00:07:48.131 --> 00:07:49.470
Oh!

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:50.780
Every time.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.140
We cannot do a paint ball video

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.490
without you doing that.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.800
Didn't get me though, really.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.013
No, just me.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:07:59.063
That's unfortunate.

00:07:59.063 --> 00:08:00.390
I've meant to have the clean lab coats.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.830
Sorry, it does come off quite easily.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.663
Does it?

00:08:02.663 --> 00:08:03.496
Yeah.

00:08:03.496 --> 00:08:04.830
Tell you what, the Blue
Man hair didn't come off.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.677
That didn't, did it?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.513
It didn't dry, either.

00:08:07.513 --> 00:08:08.430
I think you need a new lab coat.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.490
About a month later.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:10.390
I should get a new lab coat.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.170
Yeah, you should.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.413
I mean, I need one, but, I don't know.

00:08:14.413 --> 00:08:15.913
It's just not in the budget.

00:08:18.302 --> 00:08:19.370
Quite like those shots.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.260
Very satisfying to watch.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.050
Just the way the paint spreads
in, sort of, random patterns,

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.270
different every time.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.850
I could just watch them collide all day.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:28.750
Well, sometimes, I couldn't
actually tell if they'd hit.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.640
The only way I could tell was

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.380
if there was no noise on
the fence, either side.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.213
Yeah.

00:08:33.213 --> 00:08:34.262
Because there would be nothing left of it.

00:08:34.262 --> 00:08:35.490
It's just be evisceration--

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.370
Well, sometimes they would hit,

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.870
but depending on the timing, they'd hit,

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.950
sort of, over here and clip, or over here,

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.583
but they would nail each other here.

00:08:41.583 --> 00:08:44.600
But, it was interesting
because the wood is all ,

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.200
jostle-y, and the pressure
from pulling the triggers,

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.060
the barrels, as you were
pulling them, were doing that.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.880
So, I'm amazed that
they ever hit each other

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.940
because it was like .

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.290
I think they just come out so fast

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.460
that by the time the barrels
react and move around,

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:59.520
the paint balls already come out.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.230
Like, when you saw with the close-up shot

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.890
of the paint ball gun, it came out,

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.770
and then it went like whoa.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.997
This time, we didn't shoot each other,

00:09:05.997 --> 00:09:08.830
but we still made a video
with paint ball guns.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.120
That's good going.
We're evolving.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.456
We don't always have to hurt each other.

00:09:11.456 --> 00:09:12.520
No!

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:13.430
No, although, you did say,

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.263
can I shoot you in the face with it?

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:15.096
And I said no.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.033
So.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.160
That wasn't really a serious suggestion.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.320
Well, hopefully you enjoyed that video.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.726
Feel free to follow us on Twitter.

00:09:23.726 --> 00:09:24.880
Ooh!

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.240
I got myself with it!
That was a backfire.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.840
Feel free to subscribe
to the Slow Mo Guys.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.830
We do slow-mo all the time.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.060
And, also, we have a second channel

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.303
full of behind-the-scenes

00:09:33.303 --> 00:09:34.800
and extra guff.

